module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.the_occurrence_role_index_keys_atoms_the_normalized_tree_does_not_carry

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data the_occurrence_role_index_keys_atoms_the_normalized_tree_does_not_carry: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "the_occurrence_role_index_keys_atoms_the_normalized_tree_does_not_carry" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: v2.compiler.occurrence_role's role index cannot answer declaration-vs-reference for ANY site the front-end collectors record, so any consumer that gates on the role axis silently gates on nothing. The index is built over a tree and keyed by ids, and the atoms the collectors actually carry answer -- through the one keying rule -- to ids the index does not hold. A consumer that reads the absence as `not a declaration` gets the WRONG ANSWER FOR EVERY BINDER, and a consumer that reads it as `not a reference` gets the wrong answer for every free name. Either reading is a decoration, not a check.",
    "MEASURED (PR #14435, 2026-10-19, claim_batch --claim-run over src/v2/test/claim/lexical_scope.dag on the remote runner). Specimen `fn u(chars: fn(String) -> Int, x: String) -> Int { let chars = x  chars(s: x) }`: every recorded site reads role `none`, binder sites included. Six binder-kind controls were authored for this row and all six FAIL, which IS the restoration evidence named here: v2.test.claim.lexical_scope occurrence_role_completeness_fn_param_binder_reads_declaration, occurrence_role_completeness_let_binder_reads_declaration, occurrence_role_completeness_field_declaration_binder_reads_declaration, occurrence_role_completeness_generic_parameter_binder_reads_declaration, occurrence_role_completeness_match_pattern_binder_reads_declaration, occurrence_role_completeness_lambda_parameter_binder_reads_declaration. They are NOT left in the tree red: a red control asserts nothing, and a no-op gate reads as if the declaration cell were closed. They land with the repair.",
    "L1 -- THE INDEX KEYS A CHILD THE NORMALIZED TREE DOES NOT CARRY. v2.compiler.occurrence_role roles_walk records a name only for the child that answers v2.std.grammar parse_production_emitted_identity_optional, and record_name takes that node's OccurrenceMinted id. The emitted-production-identity annotation is a PARSE-TREE fact: the normalized tree the collectors walk does not carry the annotated atoms, so the index ends up keyed by ids no recorded site has. Counting the annotation in both trees for one module is the witness (wit_role_keying, the same run).",
    "L2 -- THE INDEX POPULATION IS TINY AND DISJOINT FROM THE SITE IDS. For the specimen above the index holds a handful of entries (the fn name, the two parameter binders, one argument label) against ~14 recorded sites, and none of its keys is the id a recorded site answers with. Consistent with the earlier probe over the same fixture: PARSE-ROLES reported 4 keyed occurrences over a 129-identity parse tree (14=DECL:callable, 16=DECL:value, 50=DECL:value, 82=REF:value -- the last is the ARGUMENT LABEL `s`), and NORM-ROLES reported 0. The single ReferenceRole-producing rows in the name table are two LABEL rows (field_init and arg), which is why no ordinary value reference is keyed either.",
    "WHY IT MATTERS, CONCRETELY. The cell that needs this axis is the LET BINDER: `let chars = x` is DeclarationRole at a VALUE position, so no position variant can exclude it and the position repair in #14435 does not reach it. A sweep gating only on position would import `std.host_text { chars }` into the module that binds `chars` itself -- the #14338 mis-edit, in a different spelling. That cell is therefore still held ONLY by #14338's interim guard (v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep roster_name_locally_bound, whose roster_node_binds covers bind_binder), which is why the guard must not be dissolved before this row closes: it is not a second path beside a modelled one, it is the only authority for that cell.",
    "WHAT WAS NOT THE DEFECT, SO NOBODY RE-DERIVES IT. Two premises were measured and discarded: (i) normalize does NOT re-mint authored identities -- src/v2/compiler/normalize.dag constructs no OccurrenceMinted at all (its single occurrence is a read arm), node_rebuild copies the identity, and allocate_pending_here (v2.std.node) converts OccurrencePending to OccurrenceProjected WITH its cause; (ii) nothing in v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold mints an authored atom either (its two OccurrenceMinted mentions are read arms; the binder-atom builders take the atom as an INPUT). The only mint in production is v1_compiler_parse.rs's call of std_occurrence_identity.rs node_occurrence_identity_minted, in the PARSE layer. So identity is preserved; it is the KEYING that fails.",
    "THE ONE KEYING RULE IS ALREADY SOUNDED AND ALREADY SHARED, SO THE REPAIR IS NOT A NEW MECHANISM. std.occurrence_identity authored_occurrence_of answers the authored occurrence an identity stands for: OccurrenceMinted by its own id, OccurrenceProjected and OccurrencePending by their cause, ONE STEP (a ScopedOccurrenceRef carries a raw OccurrenceId, so the substrate allows no further hop), OccurrenceSynthetic nothing. It was written inside v2.compiler.reference_conservation and moved to std.occurrence_identity in #14435 so the conservation audit and the role reader share one rule; reference_conservation holds at 26/26 with byte-identical eval_steps across that move. The repair is to key the index so that the atoms the collectors carry are in it, and to read sites through that one rule -- not to add a second index, a second keying function, or a permissive default.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- the axis was authored, then MEASURED before it was trusted, and the gate was removed from #14435 rather than shipped as a no-op. That measurement is the only reason the defect is not now load-bearing: a role conjunct would have compiled, would have passed every existing claim, and would have excluded nothing. HARM if missed: every declaration-vs-reference gate in the compiler reads as if it worked while admitting all sites, so a future consumer would conclude a binder is a free name and generate an import that shadows it -- the #14317 and #14338 mis-edits, at sweep scale.",
    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed. A consumer should be able to ask ONE question -- what role does the name table assign this occurrence -- and get an answer for every atom the front end can emit, keyed by the one keying rule, with absence meaning the table names no verdict rather than absence meaning `reference`. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: the v2.compiler.occurrence_role index keys EVERY binder atom the front end emits, read through std.occurrence_identity authored_occurrence_of, proven by the six binder-kind controls named above going green (each reading DeclarationRole through that rule) while reference_conservation stays 26/26 with byte-identical eval_steps. At that point #14435's roster gate may take its role conjunct and #14338's interim guard may be dissolved.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.occurrence_role", decl_name: "roles_walk", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.occurrence_role", decl_name: "record_name", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.occurrence_role", decl_name: "occurrence_role_index", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.grammar", decl_name: "parse_production_emitted_identity_optional", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.occurrence_identity", decl_name: "authored_occurrence_of", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep", decl_name: "roster_site_is_free", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.workflow.roster_import_sweep", decl_name: "roster_name_locally_bound", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.reference_conservation", decl_name: "occurrence_identity_index", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
